# =============================================================================
# Smart Sentinel AI — .dockerignore
# Keep build context small and free of secrets.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets & local env ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials*

# --- VCS ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Python build / cache ---
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info
.eggs
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.tox
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
coverage.xml

# --- Virtualenvs ---
.venv
venv
env

# --- IDE / editor ---
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# --- Claude / agent tooling ---
.claude
memory

# --- Data (heavy + non-redistributable) ---
data/*.csv
data/*.parquet
data/*.feather
data/*.h5
data/*.pkl
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- Models (rebuild from training pipeline) ---
models/
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
*.onnx
*.joblib
*.lgb
*.pickle

# --- Replay / backtest artifacts ---
replay_*.json
replay_*.csv
replay_diagnostic*
backtest_*.csv
backtest_*.json
reports/
mockups/
"Script collab"

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log

# --- Tests (not needed for production runtime) ---
tests/
test_*.py
*_test.py

# --- Docs (kept out of runtime image) ---
docs/
# ...EXCEPT the legal documents, which are not documentation: they are DATA the
# running service serves. `src/api/routes/legal.py` reads docs/legal/*.md to
# answer /api/v1/terms, /api/v1/legal/conditions and /api/v1/privacy, and
# `src/intelligence/chatbot/demo_agent.py` quotes the terms into M.I.A's product
# knowledge. Excluded, those routes answer 503 and the customer cannot read the
# contract they are asked to accept before paying.
# A `!` line re-includes a subpath of an excluded directory: unlike .gitignore,
# .dockerignore matches each full path against every pattern in order and the
# LAST match wins, so this exception is honoured even though `docs/` precedes it.
!docs/legal/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Misc ---
node_modules
# Nested JS deps/build output (e.g. webapp/) must never enter the backend
# build context — they add hundreds of MB and are irrelevant to the API image.
**/node_modules
**/.next
webapp/
dist
build
*.tar.gz
*.zip
